From c74c842bf321edf16612595c71de81d8c756d1d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 19:07:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0102 -- no unchanged-frame check on frames
 over 100,000 bytes

The first 0100 cells on AGS Quest (16-bit, 460,800-byte frame) LOST
fps_p50 (9.58 -> 7.40) while gaining p95 (9.86 -> 13.42): patch 0100
let the unchanged-frame skip engage on a bordered frame, and on a frame
that size the check itself -- a full read plus, on every changed frame,
a full copy into the cache -- costs 36.8 ms at the 486's 17 MB/s
(measured, present_dirty_check x 1233). Moving phases paid it on every
frame; static phases saved a ~59 ms present. The gate is on moving
content. Frames above 100,000 bytes now present without the check, as
they did before 0091; 320x200/320x240 8-bit frames (64,000/76,800 B,
where the check is ~6 ms against a ~76 ms present) keep it. The real
answer for big frames is the engine's own knowledge of what it drew
(P2.4), not a byte compare.
---
 Engine/gfx/ali3dsw.cpp | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Engine/gfx/ali3dsw.cpp b/Engine/gfx/ali3dsw.cpp
index 0045dd854..6d3a3a341 100644
--- a/Engine/gfx/ali3dsw.cpp
+++ b/Engine/gfx/ali3dsw.cpp
@@ -1110,7 +1110,22 @@ void SDLRendererGraphicsDriver::Present(int xoff, int yoff, GraphicFlip flip)
          _marginsCleanH == win_surface->h &&
          _marginsCleanDst.x == dst.x && _marginsCleanDst.y == dst.y &&
          _marginsCleanDst.w == dst.w && _marginsCleanDst.h == dst.h);
-    const bool clean_case = skip_allowed && (flip == kFlip_None) &&
+    // DOS-PORT patch 0102: the unchanged-frame check is only worth running
+    // on a SMALL frame. It costs a full read of the frame plus, whenever
+    // the frame did change, a full copy of it into the cache -- at the
+    // 486's 17 MB/s that is ~37 ms for AGS Quest's 460,800-byte 16-bit
+    // frame (measured, AQ100B1: present_dirty_check 36.8 ms x 1233), paid
+    // on EVERY moving frame to save a ~59 ms present on the static ones.
+    // On AGS Quest that turned a 9.6 fps_p50 into 7.4 (moving phases
+    // slower, static phases faster: p95 went 9.9 -> 13.4). For a 76,800-
+    // byte 8-bit frame the same check is ~6 ms against a ~76 ms present,
+    // which is the case patch 0091 was measured on. So: frames above
+    // 100,000 bytes are presented without the check, as before 0091; the
+    // real answer for big frames is the engine's own knowledge of what
+    // it drew (the 40/40 plan's P2.4), not a byte compare.
+    const size_t frame_bytes_for_skip = (size_t)blit_src->pitch * (size_t)blit_src->h;
+    const bool small_enough_to_check = frame_bytes_for_skip <= 100000u;
+    const bool clean_case = skip_allowed && small_enough_to_check && (flip == kFlip_None) &&
         (blit_src->format == win_surface->format) && dst_inside && margins_clean;
     if (clean_case)
     {
